<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.cobalt.seat-usage</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/cobalt/.local/bin</string>
        <!-- RULING 7 / Charter §8.4: every plist carries COBALT_ENV. This
             job writes its own F17 row into the LIVE jobs table, so it
             declares production. Without this the store would refuse to
             resolve a database at all rather than quietly defaulting to
             dev — which is the whole point of the ruling. -->
        <key>COBALT_ENV</key>
        <string>production</string>
        <!-- The REPORT is a repo file (docs/40 - DevDocs/reports/), not a
             vault note — see cobalt.vault.REPO_OWNED_ROOTS. The override
             is set anyway, and for a specific reason: a production
             process is REFUSED any target outside the production vault,
             so a future step here that does write a note must land in the
             real vault rather than failing at 06:00 on a Monday (NN#16). -->
        <key>COBALT_VAULT_PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/cobalt/Vault/Think</string>
    </dict>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <!-- ABSOLUTE PATH, deliberately: launchd posix_spawn()s
             ProgramArguments[0] and does NOT search the job's own PATH
             the way a shell does. A bare "uv" here produces exit 78
             (EX_CONFIG) with empty stdout and stderr, which is exactly
             how the 05:15 prefill failed silently on 2026-09-03. -->
        <string>/Users/cobalt/.local/bin/uv</string>
        <string>run</string>
        <string>cobalt</string>
        <string>seat-usage</string>
        <string>run</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/cobalt/cobalt</string>
    <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- HOURLY, INSIDE A WINDOW, EVERY DAY. launchd has no such shape:
         StartInterval never stops, and StartCalendarInterval is a list of
         moments. So the window is EXPANDED here into one entry per
         firing — 18 hours x 7 days = 126 entries.

         The window and the cadence are NOT literals. They are the
         tunables rows `seat_usage.window` (06:00-23:00) and
         `seat_usage.interval_min` (60), which the registry's schedule
         reads (F16); this array is generated from
         `Schedule.calendar_entries()` and the test suite compares the two
         entry-for-entry. launchd cannot read a tunables row, so a mirror
         is unavoidable — a mirror nobody checks is what is avoidable.

         WHY IT STOPS AT 23:00. The hours outside are not "cheap to
         cover": a run there rewrites the day's row with no new data and
         puts a diff in the audit log for nothing.

         WHY EVERY DAY INCLUDING WEEKENDS. Seats are used on Saturdays,
         and a Saturday's spend is exactly as real as a Tuesday's. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>0</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
